From: H96 M9 Audio Fix <fix@h96m9.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: sai: bound DAI rate and cap channels_max by tdm-lanes

The RK SAI driver advertises playback/capture.channels_max = 512.
When the CPU DAI is paired with rockchip,dummy-codec (channels_max = 384),
ASoC reports a link that can carry up to 64 channels on some vendor
kernels.  PulseAudio/WirePlumber clients then open hw_params with 64
channels, which makes rockchip_sai_hw_params() compute
  bclk = fw_ratio * slot_width * (channels / lanes) * rate
With slot_width=32, lanes=1 and channels=64 this gives bclk = 98.304 MHz,
far above the 12.288 MHz mclk -> "Mismatch mclk: ... at least 98304000"
and hw_params fails.

For boards where the physical codec is stereo-only (e.g. H96 M9 HT5010
3.5mm jack on SAI1 SDO2), the real max channel count is lanes*2.  When
rockchip,tdm-tx-lanes / rockchip,tdm-rx-lanes are explicitly set in DT,
cap playback/capture channels_max accordingly so ALSA/PipeWire never
offer more channels than the hardware can actually use.

Signed-off-by: H96 M9 Audio Fix <fix@h96m9.local>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
@@ -1230,6 +1230,18 @@
 		dai->playback.channels_min = 1;
 		dai->playback.channels_max = 512;
 		dai->playback.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_CONTINUOUS;
+		dai->playback.rate_min = 8000;
+		dai->playback.rate_max = 384000;
+		/*
+		 * If DT pins the lane count, advertise a matching max channel
+		 * count.  rockchip_sai_lanes_auto() picks 1 lane per stereo pair,
+		 * so tx_lanes*2 is the practical maximum for I2S/TDM stereo use.
+		 * Without this, dummy-codec's 384ch max makes ALSA expose 64ch,
+		 * and PipeWire/PA clients open with 64ch -> bclk overflow.
+		 */
+		if (sai->tx_lanes > 0 &&
+		    dai->playback.channels_max > sai->tx_lanes * 2)
+			dai->playback.channels_max = sai->tx_lanes * 2;
 		dai->playback.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S8 |
 					SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 					SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |
@@ -1246,6 +1258,15 @@
 		dai->capture.channels_min = 1;
 		dai->capture.channels_max = 512;
 		dai->capture.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_CONTINUOUS;
+		dai->capture.rate_min = 8000;
+		dai->capture.rate_max = 384000;
+		/*
+		 * Same as playback: if rx_lanes is pinned in DT, cap the
+		 * advertised max channels to lanes*2.
+		 */
+		if (sai->rx_lanes > 0 &&
+		    dai->capture.channels_max > sai->rx_lanes * 2)
+			dai->capture.channels_max = sai->rx_lanes * 2;
 		dai->capture.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S8 |
 				       SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 				       SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |

